        "title": "Error reports requested amount as the limit instead of guest memory size",
        "explanation": "TooMuchMemoryRequested's display is \"Requested memory should be less than {0}MiB\", but here {0} is the requested amount_mib, not the limit mem_size_mib(mem). A 4096 MiB request on a 2048 MiB guest gives \"Requested memory should be less than 4096MiB\", which misstates the limit to API users.",
        "suggestion": "Pass the limit, e.g. `BalloonError::TooMuchMemoryRequested(u32::try_from(mem_size_mib(mem)).unwrap_or(u32::MAX))`.",
